EmailTemplate.textOnly:
Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

Congratulations on your admission to Arizona State University! Thank you for contacting me with your question about the enrollment term on your admission letter.

There is no reason to be concerned that your letter states you are admitted for the summer term. All incoming freshmen admitted to the fall semester are technically admitted to the preceding summer term in order to allow them to take classes prior to their first semester. Of course, this is optional. The majority of freshmen wait to take their first courses in the fall, but you have the option to start in the summer. Visit summer sessions for new fall students for more information (https://students.asu.edu/summer/newstudents).

Everything else on your account (including registration for housing and orientation, when the time comes) applies to your fall admission.

Please let me know if you have any additional questions about your admission or the enrollment process.

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}


If you would like any additional information or have questions related to this subject, please reply to this email.

{!Case.Thread_Id}
